{
  "_doc": [
    "Shared by the capture script (writes raw/) and scripts/screenshots/frame.mjs (writes appstore/<App Store language>/).",
    "Capture needs only: iphone[].id + iphone[].theme -> raw/<lang>/iphone/<theme>/<id>.png at 1320x2868,",
    "and watch[].id -> raw/<lang>/watch/<id>.png at the Ultra 3 native size (422x514).",
    "The same iphone[] list is rendered again for the iPad from raw/<lang>/ipad/<theme>/<id>.png (2064x2752);",
    "a layout of phone-watch is iPhone-only, so that slide is left out of the iPad set, number and all.",
    "Framing fields: title, subtitle, note (small closing line) — each a message KEY, not text: the words live in packages/i18n/locales/<lang>/store.json (\\n = manual break) and reach frame.mjs as screenshots/i18n/<lang>.json via `bun run i18n`;",
    "layout = phone | phone-bottom | phone-watch, watch = <watch id> to compose beside the phone,",
    "bg = slide background (text colour is derived from its luminance), accent = rule colour.",
    "Devices are composited into Apple's own product bezels from screenshots/frames/.",
    "iphone[] is the numbered App Store set, in order; max 10.",
    "extras[] uses the same schema but renders to appstore/<lang>/extras/ instead: unnumbered spares,",
    "kept out of the contact sheet unless you pass --contact-sheet=all. Promote one by moving it",
    "into iphone[] (and dropping one of the ten).",
    "features = three phones side by side, left to right: {id, title, palette, theme, watch?} — title a store.creative.* key; palette a colour theme id from packages/core/src/themes.ts and theme light|dark, which pick both the capture (raw/<lang>/iphone/<palette>-<theme>/, from capture.sh --palette) and the band behind it; watch = a watch shot in front of that phone.",
    "style = \"story\" (the look since 1.1.2): the numbered iPhone set is drawn as ONE wide canvas, cut into slides, so a phone may run from one slide into the next.",
    "Cream background, serif headline (*word* in the accent), tilted phones, cards lifted out of the capture, the cat. Per shot, `story` (all positions are fractions: x and widths of the slide's width, y of its height):",
    "text: top|bottom, align: start|end; phone: [centre x, centre y, width, degrees]; watch: the same, for a phone-watch slide;",
    "cards: [{crop: [x, y, w, h] in capture pixels, or {en: [...], uk: [...]} where the languages lay out differently, at: [centre x, centre y, width, degrees]}];",
    "cat: {name (assets/siriusia/<name>.png), x (left edge), w, bottom (share of the cat's height left on the canvas) | onCard (index: sits on that card's top edge) + sink, front (drawn over the phone)}.",
    "A cat is clipped to its own slide, so its cut-off side never shows on the next one; its outline is cleaned of the cut-out halo when framed.",
    "A shot without `story` (the extras) gets the headline on top and the phone below it. The iPad set uses the words and the cat, not the cards (their crops are phone pixels).",
    "creative = the header and search results art: the slogan (store.creative.slogan / line), two phones (left/right: {id, crop}) and the cat."
  ],
